{title: Resurrecting Remixed (Live from Code Orange Revival)}
{artist: Elevation Worship}
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
Notes:
â€¢ These chords are my transcription by ear of the "Resurrecting Remixed (Live from Code Orange Revival)" version of the song "Resurrecting," by Elevation Worship, as found in this video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zgsaCS_YaFs
â€¢ These are as close to the original chords as possible for me. Maybe 95-100% accurate.
â€¢ As it is played in the Gospel Music style, often chords are played with notes in the bass other than the root of the chord, such as [C#/G#] (This would be a [C#] chord with [G#] played as a bass note.)
â€¢ These chords are intended for piano.
â€¢ When played on piano, the first inversion of chords is often used, or even just the root and third- this is especially true of the verses. Chords are also played low on the keyboard.
â€¢ Chords in parenthesis, such as [G#m7/B]), indicate a walking bass part. Upon this type of chord, only the bass should voice a new sound, the chord should ring out over the bass change.

